 OpenMixer each of these is written down once, in omx-contract, and everything
 else reads it. The declarations are plain JSON with a JSON Schema.
 .
 This package holds the omx-contract command, which validates, formats and
 renders the declarations, and reads the contract directory the packages
 install their definitions into as one checked set. It carries the npm
 packages it runs on (ajv and its dependencies), so it needs node and
 nothing else.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

